{
  "id": "murphy-shakti-caudate-parietal-bilateral-fast",
  "name": "8 Coil Shakti caudate signal, parietal, both sides (fast alternation, 30 min)",
  "category": "body",
  "evidence": "anecdote",
  "origin": "Todd Murphy (8 Coil Shakti software)",
  "uT": 1,
  "summary": "Murphy's caudate nucleus ('body') signal over both parietal lobes with the 8 Coil Shakti's fast alternation: on each side two coil pairs take turns twice a second. Murphy presents it for body awareness and balance and reports tingling and sensations of movement.",
  "setting": "Darkness and quiet (the vendor says effects during a session need darkness and silence); eyes closed, relaxed, without meditating or falling asleep; no meditation, mind machines or drugs at the same time.",
  "schedule": "Vendor's Shakti rules: at most every 72 h or once a week, never on consecutive days; a series of 3 or 6 sessions, then a 21-day break; try a session 2-3 times before changing it. Keep to it even though parietal thresholds are higher, and stay with parietal placement for the whole series.",
  "notes": "Coils over the parietal strip, which the vendor locates 'about an inch behind the topmost point on the head, and then in a strip down to the top of the ears': CP1, CP3, CP5 and P3 on the left, CP2, CP4, CP6 and P4 on the right (an inference). The 8 Coil Shakti puts both stereo channels on each side (in its temporal-lobe chart one channel's pair sits top and bottom, the other's front and back, each pair one + and one − coil) and alternates the signal between the channels, not between the hemispheres. How the pairs sit over the parietal lobes is not documented, so this file pairs them the same way (an inference): CP1 and CP5 (top and bottom) with CP2 and CP6 as one channel, CP3 and P3 (front and back) with CP4 and P4 as the other. Both hemispheres get every burst; the two pairs on each side take turns. Coil polarity follows that chart, carried over to these sites (an inference): on the left the top (CP1) and front (CP3) coils are − and the bottom (CP5) and back (P3) coils +; on the right the top (CP2) and front (CP4) coils are + and the bottom (CP6) and back (P4) coils −. The − coils have negative weights, which reverse their current as if the coil were turned over; + is taken as this helmet's normal drive. Fast alternation: the channels switch 'twice each second' (the vendor says fast alternation emerged as 'the most effective' in the original developers' lab tests); here the signal is gated in point tables so that the two pairs take turns every 0.5 s, and each 0.69-s burst is split between them. So that the half-second clock and the signal repeat together, a burst comes every 4.5 s (3.81 s of silence instead of Shakti's standard 4 s), and the bursts alternately start on the top/bottom and on the front/back pairs. The caudate signal is unpublished, and Murphy calls it 'not a well tested signal'; the built-in accelerating burst (6 to 30 Hz, 230 points of 3 ms = 0.69 s) stands in for it, as in the project's Shiva caudate session, so the waveform here does not differ from the amygdala stand-in. Murphy describes 'intense tingly sensations ... sensations of movement' with parietal sessions, left-side caudate sessions as arousing (energy, excitement, possibly anger or sexual desire) and right-side ones as relaxing (calm, possibly lethargy), and bilateral ones as balancing body awareness; these are vendor reports. Other forms: murphy-shakti-caudate-parietal-bilateral-slow, -left (arousal) and -right (relaxation). The vendor says thresholds over the parietal lobes 'are a bit higher' and asks users to keep to the normal schedules and not to switch back and forth between the parietal lobes and other locations. A report of anger in two users after a left caudate session followed by a left amygdala session is credited to Murphy but could not be verified on his pages (including both caudate pages); as a precaution, do not follow a left caudate session with a left amygdala session. The vendor does not suggest the caudate signal over the frontal lobes in the 2- and 4-coil Shakti. Independent double-blind tests of God-Helmet-type fields found no field effect (Granqvist 2005; Gendle & McGrath 2012, the latter with the 8 Coil Shakti amygdala signal). Not for people with epilepsy; stop at once if distressed.",
  "targets": [
    "caudate-nucleus",
    "left-supramarginal-gyrus",
